  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>First step of the reaction is dehydrohalogenation and then ozonolysis.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/491fd501-7427-495f-af2b-bd02dccdd36a-image.png\" style=\"width: 450px; height: 288px;\" /></p><p>The dehydrohalogenation of alkyl halides, another &szlig; elimination reaction, involves the loss of a hydrogen and a halide from an alkyl halide (RX). Dehydrohalogenation is normally accomplished by reacting the alkyl halide with a strong base, such as sodium ethoxide.</p>",
